1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,258
This tutorial covers penalties, fines and
maintenance recharges: how they are

2
00:00:04,258 --> 00:00:08,517
proposed, how finance decides them, and
the journal each decision writes.

3
00:00:08,517 --> 00:00:12,388
As the Company Admin, open Settings, then
Rent and fines.

4
00:00:12,388 --> 00:00:17,033
Cheque-failure fines are set once for the
organisation: 500 for a bounced

5
00:00:17,033 --> 00:00:21,679
cheque, 500 for a signature mismatch, and
1,000 for a closed account.

6
00:00:21,679 --> 00:00:26,324
A penalty is proposed automatically after
2 returned cheques on one contract;

7
00:00:26,324 --> 00:00:30,970
proposing one when rent clears late is a
separate switch, off here.

8
00:00:30,970 --> 00:00:34,066
These rules only propose; nothing posts by
itself.

9
00:00:34,066 --> 00:00:38,712
Now, as the Accountant, open Cheque and
Cash Collection and choose Penalties.

10
00:00:38,712 --> 00:00:41,035
The Proposed tab holds two items.

11
00:00:41,035 --> 00:00:44,906
Mohammed Al Rashid's June instalment
cleared after the grace period,

12
00:00:44,906 --> 00:00:48,390
so a late payment penalty of 250 was
raised.

13
00:00:48,390 --> 00:00:51,874
Hana Yoshida's is a maintenance recharge
of 800, raised

14
00:00:51,874 --> 00:00:55,358
from ticket TKT-26/1 for a cracked balcony
glass panel.

15
00:00:55,358 --> 00:00:58,842
Next to Approve, Waive would drop a
proposed item

16
00:00:58,842 --> 00:01:02,326
without posting anything, and Reduce would
lower the amount.

17
00:01:02,326 --> 00:01:04,262
Approve Mohammed's penalty, dated today.

18
00:01:04,262 --> 00:01:06,972
Approval is the only step that posts.

19
00:01:06,972 --> 00:01:09,294
Approve Hana's recharge the same way.

20
00:01:09,294 --> 00:01:12,391
Now open Journal Voucher and filter to
PEN.

21
00:01:12,391 --> 00:01:17,037
Mohammed's journal debits Rent Receivable
and credits Rent Penalty with 250, so

22
00:01:17,037 --> 00:01:21,682
he now owes it, and it is collected like
any other charge.

23
00:01:21,682 --> 00:01:25,940
Hana's debits Rent Receivable and credits
Maintenance Charges with 800: the

24
00:01:25,940 --> 00:01:30,199
landlord paid for the repair, and the
tenant pays it back.

25
00:01:30,199 --> 00:01:34,070
Back in Penalties, the Approved tab now
lists three items,

26
00:01:34,070 --> 00:01:37,554
including Layla Nasser's 500 fine for her
returned cheque.

27
00:01:37,554 --> 00:01:39,490
Each approved item offers Reverse.

28
00:01:39,490 --> 00:01:43,361
Reversing posts the mirror image of its
journal, so a

29
00:01:43,361 --> 00:01:47,232
mistake is corrected in the books and
nothing is deleted.
